WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.760
Some movies are seemingly cursed, and everything
that could possibly go wrong does go wrong.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.340
Take, for example, Chaos Walking.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.660
Starring Spider-Man and Rey, aka Tom Holland
and Daisy Ridley, it should be a sure-fire

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:11.400
crowd-pleaser.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.800
So why has the studio declared it unreleasable?

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.980
Chaos Walking is based on a trilogy of books
by novelist Patrick Ness.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.220
The story takes place on an alien planet called
New World, settled by Puritan-like humans

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:26.260
who left what's presumably Earth more than
20 years before the events of the first book,

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:27.900
The Knife of Never Letting Go.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.560
On this planet, all living beings can hear
and see one another's thoughts in the form

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:36.760
of an unrelenting cacophony of images, words,
and sounds, which everyone accurately calls

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:37.260
"Noise."

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.480
In other words, it's chaos walking.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.100
"What if you couldn't get away?

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.100
What if you really couldn't get away?

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.140
What if there was no escape?"

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.800
As the plot unfolds, a teenager named Todd
finds a place where there is no Noise.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:52.370
He flees the male-only settlement of Prentisstown
and meets a woman named Viola, which is remarkable,

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:55.060
as nobody knew there were any non-males on
New World.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.860
Eventually there's a showdown between human
settlers and the intelligent native race called

00:00:58.860 --> 00:00:59.440
the Spackle.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:03.960
In 2016, it was reported that Tom Holland
was cast to play Todd and Daisy Ridley was

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.020
all set to play Viola.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:10.440
Lionsgate grabbed the rights to adapt and
produce a Chaos Walking film way back in 2011.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.260
At the time, the studio had carved out a lucrative
niche for itself as the company that made

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:18.820
all the major big-screen versions of super-popular
young adult novel franchises.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:22.780
Having already brought Twilight from the bookstore
to the multiplex and with the first Hunger

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:26.500
Games movie on the way, Chaos Walking seemed
like the next logical step.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.980
Some major players started to surround the
project.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:33.139
Robert Zemeckis, the filmmaker behind Back
to the Future and Forrest Gump, was supposed

00:01:33.139 --> 00:01:37.219
to direct, but that deal ultimately fell apart,
though he remained on as a producer.

00:01:37.219 --> 00:01:40.539
It was perhaps a sign of trouble to come that
there was apparently a struggle to find a

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.969
director to commit to a project with so much
potential.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:47.200
A long five years after announcing the project,
Lionsgate revealed that filming could begin

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.640
in the fall of 2016, now with Doug Liman in
the director's chair.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:56.460
With Liman behind the camera, filming on Chaos
Walking finally commenced in August 2017 in

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:56.960
Montreal.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:01.139
By that time, the rest of the cast had been
filled out, with such notable names as David

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.940
Oyelowo, Demian Bichir, Mads Mikkelsen, and
Nick Jonas.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.849
The shoot seemingly went well, but the result
of the tireless and expensive efforts of cast

00:02:08.849 --> 00:02:11.440
and crew didn't quite meet studio expectations.

00:02:11.629 --> 00:02:15.400
According to Lionsgate employees close to
the situation, the first cut of Chaos Walking

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:19.360
turned out so badly that studio executives
deemed it, quote, "unreleasable."

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:23.579
It had cost a staggering $100 million, but
it was apparently so awful once assembled

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.320
that it wasn't fit for public consumption.

00:02:25.549 --> 00:02:29.860
So Lionsgate canceled the film's scheduled
March 2019 release and ordered up extensive

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.760
reshoots that would cost millions and take
three weeks to film.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:37.799
If studios invest a fortune in a major movie
and a rough cut seems lackluster, it makes

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.080
sense to spend a few more million on reshoots.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.660
In recent years, for example, Justice League
and Shazam! have made headlines for re-assembling

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:49.140
casts and crews to film extensive new scenes
not long before their scheduled theatrical

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:49.640
releases.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:54.020
To generate new script pages for Chaos Walking,
Lionsgate hired Patrick Ness, the novels'

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:54.520
author.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:58.720
While Ness likely had relatively little trouble
pinpointing just what was missing from the

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.320
adaptation, actually filming those scenes
proved difficult.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:05.819
Reshoot plans were announced in April 2018,
but cameras didn't start to roll until April

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:06.500
2019.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:11.189
The reason was that in the time after principal
photography wrapped, the careers of stars

00:03:11.189 --> 00:03:13.450
Tom Holland and Daisy Ridley exploded.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:17.799
Ultimately, there was a gap of about 18 months
between the first and last scenes shot.

00:03:17.799 --> 00:03:22.180
Holland and Ridley don't quite look like teenagers
anymore, meaning that they would appear strikingly

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.680
and distractingly different from scene to
scene.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:29.900
When Lionsgate kicked off pre-production on
Chaos Walking in 2011, sweeping movie series

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.939
based on bestselling young adult sagas were
all the rage.

00:03:32.939 --> 00:03:38.050
The four Hunger Games films took in more than
$1.4 billion at the domestic box office, while

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:41.040
the likes of The Maze Runner and Divergent
also performed well.

00:03:41.209 --> 00:03:45.060
But within a couple of years, the dystopian
young adult trend was starting to lose its

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:45.560
luster.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.240
The third Divergent movie did so poorly at
the box office that a wrap-up finale was canceled,

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:53.420
and standalone adaptations like The 5th Wave
bombed hard.

00:03:53.529 --> 00:03:57.400
By the time production on Chaos Walking began
in earnest in 2016, the writing was on the

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:00.680
wall that this was a movie past its sell-by
date.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:04.120
But there are still plans to get it into theaters
at some point!

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:07.930
As of summer 2019, it's tentatively scheduled
for release in 2020.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:12.300
But for now, it remains a film in limbo, as
confusing as the chaos in its title.

